---
title: See what a match looks like before signing in
date: 2026-07-29
summary: Job cards now show a blurred preview of the profile match — built from that job's real skills, not a stock example.
type: changelog
tags:
  - profile-match
  - job-seekers
---

If you are signed in with skills on your profile, every job card shows how much of the
posting you already cover: a green-and-red bar and a percentage. Signed out, that corner
of the card was simply empty — you had no way to tell the feature existed, let alone
whether it was worth an account.

Now it shows a blurred preview. The skills in it are the ones the posting actually asks
for, tinted as "you have this" or "you don't", with a coverage bar above them. The
numbers are a placeholder — nobody can compute your match before you have a profile —
so they are blurred, and the same preview sits on the job page under **Profile match**
with a way in.

The salary stays sharp. So do the skill names, near enough to read: the blur is there to
mark the figures as not-yours-yet, not to hide what the job wants.

The **Analyze match** offer under it is visible too now — the deeper read of your CV
against the role, with gaps and ATS flags. Pressing it asks you to sign in first, since
it needs a CV to read.

Sign in and the preview is replaced by the real thing — your skills against that
posting's, counted exactly, with the ones you are missing named.
